				<u>SIG</u>
				1018.4
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>). (Usu. second declension,
			prob. by 'contamination' of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινίκιος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικοῦς;</span> once third declension, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικιοῦντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Col.</u>
					796a32
				</span></i>
			, prob. by 'contamination' of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινίκιος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικόεις.</span>) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικιοῦν, τό</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαστήριον</span>),  a court of
			justice at Athens, named from the colour of its walls, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.28.8
			</span></i>.</div>
